\revision{The best-observed results in \mbox{\tabref{tab:generalization}} show that the proposed method achieves Final scores of 78.98 and 77.49 for monocular and binocular evaluation on On-site, respectively, and 55.35 on EDID, outperforming all comparison methods on these target-domain metrics. The improvements over the strongest DG comparator for each metric are 0.85, 0.94, and 1.47 points, respectively.}

\revision{\mbox{\tabref{tab:generalization-top5}} further shows that the proposed method achieves mean Final scores of 78.11 $\pm$ 0.84 and 76.27 $\pm$ 1.25 for monocular and binocular evaluation on On-site, respectively, and 54.41 $\pm$ 1.06 on EDID, again the highest among the compared methods. On RFMiD, its best-observed result and candidate mean both exceed those of ResNet50, MixStyle, and RSC, with FACT attaining the highest values in this direction. Together, the two tables demonstrate the recognition advantage of the proposed method in eight-class ODIR generalization and shared-class cross-dataset evaluation on EDID through both its best-observed performance and its average performance across candidate checkpoints.}

